From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tim2tox-bootstrap <bootstrap@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] V2TIMMessageManager.reSendMessage: route through the
 platform like sendMessage

0003 routed `sendMessage`, `createForwardMessage`, `findMessages`,
`downloadMessage`, ... through `TencentCloudChatSdkPlatform` whenever
`isPlatformRouted` is true, but left `reSendMessage` on its upstream
`kIsWeb`-only branch. With a custom platform installed (Tim2ToxSdkPlatform)
a resend therefore took the binary-replacement path:

  TIMMessageManager.reSendMessage -> findMessages -> DartFindMessages
    -> V2TIMMessageManagerImpl::FindMessages (always empty: C++ keeps no
       history) -> "message not found", data == null

so tapping the retry glyph on ANY failed bubble (C2C or group, text or
media) always failed, and UIKit, which had already swapped the failed row
for a SENDING copy and only reconciles when `data != null`, left the
bubble spinning forever. The platform has a complete `reSendMessage`
(rebuilds the message, including media, from the failed-message store);
it was simply unreachable.

diff --git a/lib/manager/v2_tim_message_manager.dart b/lib/manager/v2_tim_message_manager.dart
index d257a16..1957a8b 100644
--- a/lib/manager/v2_tim_message_manager.dart
+++ b/lib/manager/v2_tim_message_manager.dart
@@ -1910,7 +1910,7 @@ class V2TIMMessageManager {
     bool onlineUserOnly = false,
     Object? webMessageInstatnce
   }) async {
-    if (kIsWeb) {
+    if (TencentCloudChatSdkPlatform.instance.isPlatformRouted) {
       return await TencentCloudChatSdkPlatform.instance
           .reSendMessage(msgID: msgID, onlineUserOnly: onlineUserOnly, webMessageInstatnce: webMessageInstatnce);
     }
